  "lean": {
    "statement": "\n    {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]\n    [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E]\n    {V : E → ℝ} {α β : ℝ≥0} {η : ℝ}\n    (hα : 0 < (α : ℝ)) (hαβ : α ≤ β) (hV : ContDiff ℝ 2 V)\n    (hH : ∀ x a : E,\n      (α : ℝ) * ‖a‖^2 ≤ (fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x a) a ∧\n      (fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x a) a ≤ (β : ℝ) * ‖a‖^2)\n    (hη : 0 < η) (hβη : (β : ℝ) * η ≤ 1) :\n    let μ := (volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x => -V x)\n    let J := Measure.map (fun p : E × E => (p.1, p.1 + Real.sqrt η • p.2))\n      (μ.prod (stdGaussian E))\n    let ν := J.snd\n    let Λ := J.map (fun p : E × E => (p.2, (2 : ℝ) • p.1 - p.2))\n    let F := fun p : E × E => (p.1, (2 : ℝ) • p.1 - p.2)\n    let P : Lp ℝ 2 J →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 J :=\n      (lpMeas ℝ ℝ (MeasurableSpace.comap Prod.snd (inferInstance : MeasurableSpace E))\n        2 J).subtypeL ∘L condExpL2 ℝ ℝ measurable_snd.comap_le\n    IsProbabilityMeasure μ ∧ IsProbabilityMeasure J ∧ IsProbabilityMeasure ν ∧\n    ∃ R S : Kernel E E, IsMarkovKernel R ∧ IsMarkovKernel S ∧\n      (J.map Prod.swap).IsCondKernel R ∧\n      (∀ y, S y = (R y).map (fun x => (2 : ℝ) • x - y)) ∧\n      (∀ y, S y = (volume : Measure E).tilted\n        (fun u => -V ((1/2 : ℝ) • (y+u)) - ‖y-u‖^2/(8*η))) ∧\n      Λ.IsCondKernel S ∧ Λ.fst = ν ∧\n      ∃ U : Lp ℝ 2 J →ₗᵢ[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 J,\n        (∀ g : Lp ℝ 2 J, (U g : E × E → ℝ) =ᵐ[J] g ∘ F) ∧\n        Function.Involutive U ∧ IsSelfAdjoint U.toContinuousLinearMap ∧\n        let A := P * U.toContinuousLinearMap * P\n        let B := (1-P) * U.toContinuousLinearMap * P\n        let D := (1-P) * U.toContinuousLinearMap * (1-P)\n        star B * B = P - A^2 ∧ star B * D = -(A * star B) ∧\n        (∀ g : Lp ℝ 2 J, P g = g → ‖B g‖^2 = ‖g‖^2 - ‖A g‖^2) ∧\n        ∀ (f : E → ℝ), ContDiff ℝ ∞ f → HasCompactSupport f →\n          let Tf := fun y => ∫ u, f u ∂S y\n          Differentiable ℝ Tf ∧ MemLp f 2 ν ∧ MemLp Tf 2 ν ∧\n          MemLp (gradient Tf) 2 ν ∧\n          Integrable (fun y =>\n            AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.FunctionalInequalities.Poincare.variance\n              (S y) f) ν ∧\n          ∃ g : Lp ℝ 2 J,\n            (g : E × E → ℝ) =ᵐ[J] (fun p => f p.2) ∧ P g = g ∧\n            (A g : E × E → ℝ) =ᵐ[J] (fun p => Tf p.2) ∧\n            ‖g‖^2 = (∫ y, (f y)^2 ∂ν) ∧\n            ‖A g‖^2 = (∫ y, (Tf y)^2 ∂ν) ∧\n            (∫ y, AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.FunctionalInequalities.Poincare.variance\n              (S y) f ∂ν) = ‖B g‖^2 ∧\n            η * (∫ y, ‖gradient Tf y‖^2 ∂ν) ≤\n              (1-(α : ℝ)*η)^2/(4*(1+(α : ℝ)*η)) * ‖B g‖^2",
    "statement_sha256": "b0753416a337cc85246cce3f95a321b108136f577c45c6398ec2fb1876d0db18",
    "compiled": true,
    "approved_definition_context": [
      "E is a finite-dimensional real inner-product space, with norm and Borel measurable structure, including rank zero. V is globally C2 with genuine evaluated Hessian bounded below/above by positive alpha/nonnegative beta times norm-square; 0<alpha<=beta, eta>0 and beta eta<=1.",
      "volume is canonical volume. Measure.tilted uses exp of its supplied function divided by its genuine Bochner normalizer. stdGaussian E is the centered identity-covariance Gaussian. mu, J, nu, Lambda and F are literal laws/maps specified in the statement; probability is produced as output.",
      "Kernel E E is measurable; IsMarkovKernel gives probability at every fiber. IsCondKernel means actual first marginal compProd kernel equals the joint measure. One common R and S are chosen before all observations; reflection relation and explicit normalized S density hold for every y. Lambda disintegration and its marginal are output.",
      "Lp real 2 J is the actual Hilbert space of square-integrable AE classes. The displayed P is the actual L2 conditional projection onto the comap-snd measurable subspace. U is an actual real linear isometry on the SAME Hilbert space with the displayed AE reflection pullback action, involution and self-adjointness. A=PUP, B=(I-P)UP, D=(I-P)U(I-P) are local aliases. Star means actual Hilbert adjoint; multiplication is actual operator composition.",
      "The theorem outputs star B B=P-A squared, star B D=-(A star B), and the true norm defect for every macroscopic class Pg=g. No operator/law/class equality certificate is supplied as a public premise.",
      "f is a real signed globally C-infinity compactly supported function. Tf(y) is its literal Bochner integral under SAME S(y). True differentiability, f/Tf/gradient L2 under SAME nu and conditional variance L1 are all produced. gradient is inverse Riesz of the genuine real Frechet derivative.",
      "Poincare.variance(S y)f is the integral under S(y) of (f(u)-integral f dS(y)) squared. A actual class g has AE[J] representative f o snd and Pg=g; Ag has AE[J] representative Tf o snd. Both squared norms equal actual second moments under nu. Expected conditional variance equals actual squared norm of Bg.",
      "The exact energy bound is eta times actual integrated squared gradient at most (1-alpha eta)^2/[4(1+alpha eta)] times actual Bg squared norm. AE equalities denote classes only and do not assert equality of pointwise derivatives. Smooth-test output only; no arbitrary rough outer-domain or operator-root extension is asserted."
